1
00:05:13,333 --> 00:05:19,333
Sometimes You Have to Fall Before You Fly

2
00:10:26,666 --> 00:10:32,666
Full Out is a history, drama, family film directed by Sean Cisterna.

3
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:46,000
Based on the true life story of California gymnast Ariana Berlin.

4
00:20:53,333 --> 00:20:59,333
As she zoned in on her Olympic goals, 14 year old Ariana Berlin's life took a
sharp turn when she was involved in a debilitating car accident.

5
00:26:06,666 --> 00:26:12,666
Gaining her confidence and movement back through learning hip hop dance, she unexpectedly found herself
called back to the gymnastics world thanks to world renowned UCLA Coach Valorie Kondos Field.

6
00:31:20,000 --> 00:31:26,000
With Val's help, Ariana was eventually able to secure a spot on the UCLA gymnastics team and
win an NCAA championship, a lifelong goal that she had always dreamed of.

7
00:36:33,333 --> 00:36:39,333
This is a wonderfully inspiring story of persistence, confidence, and the
heart and courage to make a somewhat impossible comeback in life.

8
00:41:46,666 --> 00:41:52,666
Ariana Berlin, played by Ana Golja.

9
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:06,000
Coach Valorie Kondos-Field, played by Jennifer Beals.

10
00:52:13,333 --> 00:52:19,333
Michelle, played by Asha Bromfield.

11
00:57:26,666 --> 00:57:32,666
Nate, played by Trevor Tordjman.

12
01:02:40,000 --> 01:02:46,000
Coach Pierce, played by Jake Epstein.

13
01:07:53,333 --> 01:07:59,333
Susan Berlin, played by Ramona Milano.

14
01:13:06,666 --> 01:13:12,666
Full Out, also known as Full Out: The Ariana Berlin Movie, is a 2015 drama young-adult TV movie
directed by Sean Cisterna based on the life story of American gymnast Ariana Berlin.

15
01:18:20,000 --> 01:18:26,000
Ana Golja received a 2016 Canadian Screen Awards nomination for Best
Performance in a Children's or Youth Program or Series.

16
01:23:33,333 --> 01:23:39,333
The film explores themes of dancing, sports,
gymnastics, biography, car accident.

17
01:28:46,666 --> 01:28:52,666
The tone is uplifting and emotional.
